  "year": "1983",
  "subtitle": "A wrist-worn decompression computer that renders your body's nitrogen uptake as a row of 12 abstract 'tissue' bar graphs",
  "why_scout_cares": "The Orca Edge replaces dive tables and a dive watch with real-time wearable ambient reasoning: the diver reads a metaphor (12 horizontal tissue-saturation bars) instead of a numeric decompression plan, and infers safe ascent by which bars cross a limiting line. It is the museum's only embodied, safety-critical wearable that asks the wearer to calibrate their own physiology against a live abstract display.",
  "search_terms": ["Orca Edge", "dive computer", "decompression", "Orca Industries", "tissue bar graph", "wearable computing"],
